A glob view prints a Markdown file's frontmatter, or else its first heading as its outline line prints it; frontmatter without fields counts as none, headings in block quotes and lists are skipped, and a file without either has no header.
File mode doesn't print the heading as a header, because it is already the outline's first line.
Expected output is hand-written: the TypeScript build printed `(no header available)` without frontmatter.
== args
input
== file input/empty-frontmatter.md
---
---
Setext title
============
== file input/fields.md
---
title: Fields
---
# Not the summary
== file input/plain.md
Just text.
== file input/quoted.md
> # Quoted
- # Listed

## Usage ##
== stdout
glob view: input
Includes only a header or summary per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
input/empty-frontmatter.md: # Setext title
input/fields.md: title: "Fields"
input/plain.md: (no header available)
input/quoted.md: ## Usage
== stderr
== exit 0
